<title>FRANCE: New York top ex-Paris export destination in Nov 96.</title>
<headline>New York top ex-Paris export destination in Nov 96.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top export destination from Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports last month, despite a strong decline in traffic on 1995 levels.</p>
<p>The top ten ex-Paris air cargo destinations in November 1996 and the percentage change on November 1995, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  New York	 3,616 tonnes  down  3.2pct</p>
<p> 2  Hong Kong	2,690 tonnes  up   37.9</p>
<p> 3  Chicago	  2,433 tonnes  up   11.8</p>
<p> 4  Tokyo	    2,240 tonnes  down 18.5</p>
<p> 5  Montreal	 1,354 tonnes  down  2.8</p>
<p> 6  Mexico City    1,276 tonnes  up   30.4</p>
<p> 7  Sao Paulo	1,271 tonnes  up   37.4</p>
<p> 8  Los Angeles    1,147 tonnes  up    7.8</p>
<p> 9  Singapore	1,142 tonnes  up   91.2</p>
<p> 10 Miami		884 tonnes  up   38.1</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
